    "q-116727": {
      "dom_id": "step-q116727",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193183/assets/69245c30b32f12e59a5f57f2e8fb17c7374726ffd6db10726cb508727f66c409.png)\n\nFind the measure of angle $B$ given that $m∠A=m∠C.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using $m∠A=m∠C,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & =m∠C \\\\ 3z+{20}^{∘} & =4z \\\\ z & ={20}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, substituting $z={20}^{∘}$ in the expression for $m∠C,$ we get\n\n$$\nm∠C=4({20}^{∘})={80}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find $m∠B$ using the fact that the internal angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B+2m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B+2\\cdot {80}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B+{160}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={20}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-116727-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{18}^{∘}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"23\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.393em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2218\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>18</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
